-# PI 4.0.28 — second-ball state value
-
-Parent 1d7bf1b43a4384dff8b8ffbcb4953d18933e9393; [DES evidence](https://github.com/tvhuy99-web/Coffee-Shop-Manager-Google-AI-Studio/actions/runs/45520666910), [attribute audit](https://github.com/tvhuy99-web/Coffee-Shop-Manager-Google-AI-Studio/actions/runs/45520666555), full runtime 185 pass / 0 fail / 8 ignored, APK success, P1 legacy integration 17/22 still fails. Baseline 1000: 2.533 goals, 26.305 shots, 1211.802 passes, 71.7683% accuracy, 80.433 live minutes, 3.72 stopped tackle fouls, 45.347 commits / 886.93 candidate evaluations, 42.973 actual contacts. 3.626 controlled tackles, 8.065 loose contacts, 3.880 attack recoveries, 4.168 defence recoveries, .015 boundary. No aggregate recovery rate used as an input.
-
-Keep the existing legal-contact and foul forecasts, but split legal contact into control and loose branches using the existing contact-control equation with own defender attributes and neutral observable pressure. Forecast the conditional loose-ball trajectory using 4.0.27 contact geometry and moving-frame block law, projected challenger along the visible approach ray, current body velocities, neutral motion priors for all other players (no hidden opponent attributes or planned movement). Estimate the first reachable time per side on a bounded 2.5 s local search, soft one-second total time-difference margin around ties; no random outcome draw. No access before a predicted boundary gives no recovery credit; no access within the horizon and no boundary gives an uncertain neutral prior. The loose branch values actual prospective recovery, otherwise assumes continuation of original possession. No double counting of miss/foul, no changes to physical execution, motion integration, referee rules, pass or shot coefficients. Existing isolated legality/geometry tests keep explicit fully controlled legal-contact fixtures to preserve their original assumptions; new tests isolate the partial-control and geometry-dependent race. Existing full session tests unchanged. New matched-contact diagnostics distinguish expected controlled/loose contact and conditional recovery estimates on actual loose contacts; unresolved and boundary cases are not forced into either recovery side.
-
-Limitations: approximate subjective reach and pressure, 100 ms local samples, 25 m candidate screening, current velocities rather than unknown future plans, no separate restart/clearance value, no opponent-specific learning or post-contact action tree. The forecast may be wrong and may decrease tackle choices further; this is not a foul-frequency fix. Compare identical populations, contact-audit denominators and CI before accepting; next diagnose exposure to physical challenges, movement and foul opportunities. Policy ID changes; older policy checkpoints rejected by existing contract. No claims of realism or green CI before results.
